      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Crunch doesn't save VRAM, it only cuts down on file size. This is at the expense of loading time as the texture is uncrunched with the CPU\n\nPersonally I'd prefer ability to limit VRAM of an avatar, if it's a single 8k texture, or a pile of 1ks I don't care about those specifics.\n\nActually with mipmaps an 8k texture is trucking around with lower resolutions, so 4k, 2k, 1k, etc are accessible.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-16T02:55:20.298Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "...As I'm writing this it seems that a couple more people have this idea. But, I'm gonna write this anyway-\n\nI think it'd be a good idea to make a \"Max Texture Size\" threshold- like 1K max for avatars- or add some kind of \"Optimized Texture Compression\" mode that just throws BC7 on everything (..with or without crunch depending on the texture's original import settings. Crunch on everything would fry a CPU for like 5 minutes)\n\nI think this kinda thing is really important, once the VRAM kicks in your PC goes overdrive and your frames are eaten up. \n\n...Also I feel the need to bring up that I have a chaotic friend selling a rabbit base model with f###in' 1.3 Gb of VRAM- that's AFTER they \"optimized\"  it...so imagine like, 2 of those in one lobby....You're dead. Byebye, GPU gone lmao\n\nBut in all seriousness we need this feature, I'd happily sacrifice load-time for overall framerate :D",
